{"id":"1fb825ce951589c7cb39b51a0bb4c209960e97f6","axis":"silent","repo":"web-infra-dev/rspack","sha":"1fb825ce951589c7cb39b51a0bb4c209960e97f6","parsed":{"files":[{"path":".agents/RSPACK_SOURCES.md","lines":["@@ -79,8 +79,8 @@ Preserve these contracts:","    line and omit names. Do not build a full map and discard columns afterward."," 7. **Generated-only content is valid.** The common map builder returns `None` when encoded mappings","    are empty; this says nothing about whether content exists.","-8. **Borrowed `'static` views must retain their owner.** The lifetime extensions in `SourceMap`,","-   `CachedSource`, and `SourceContentLines` depend on explicit owner relationships.","+8. **Borrowed `'static` views must retain their owner.** The lifetime extensions in","+   `CachedSource` and `SourceContentLines` depend on explicit owner relationships."," 9. **`Source` remains `Send + Sync`.** Temporary UTF-16 indices are local to each mapping stream."," 10. **Hashing and equality describe the canonical source graph, not rendered output.**","     Persistent-cache restoration must reconstruct the same graph, including intentional","@@ -99,16 +99,15 @@ Despite its historical name:"," pub type BoxSource = Arc<dyn Source>;"," ```"," ","-| Method                | Use                                       | Cost expectations                           |","-| --------------------- | ----------------------------------------- | ------------------------------------------- |","-| `source()`            | text/binary value                         | borrowed for leaves; may flatten composites |","-| `rope(on_chunk)`      | incremental text spans                    | preserve borrowing; text-oriented           |","-| `buffer()`            | exact bytes                               | preferred for binary data                   |","-| `size()`              | output byte length                        | must match buffer/writer length             |","-| `map(options)`        | map borrowing from `self`                 | direct borrow or one streamed rebuild       |","-| `map_static(options)` | map that outlives the local source borrow | retains an `Arc` owner                      |","-| `update_hash()`       | structural hash                           | cached by `CachedSource`                    |","-| `to_writer()`         | incremental byte output                   | preferred for emission                      |","+| Method           | Use                     | Cost expectations                             |","+| ---------------- | ----------------------- | --------------------------------------------- |","+| `source()`       | text/binary value       | borrowed for leaves; may flatten composites   |","+| `rope(on_chunk)` | incremental text spans  | preserve borrowing; text-oriented             |","+| `buffer()`       | exact bytes             | preferred for binary data                     |","+| `size()`         | output byte length      | must match buffer/writer length               |","+| `map(options)`   | independently owned map | share an existing map or one streamed rebuild |","+| `update_hash()`  | structural hash         | cached by `CachedSource`                      |","+| `to_writer()`    | incremental byte output | preferred for emission                        |"," "," For every implementation:"," ","@@ -142,7 +141,7 @@ only mapping metadata is needed, and a mapping can have no original location."," mutability. `get_map` sets it to `true`. `ReplaceSource` requests `false` because it must split"," actual spans."," ","-A bare `SourceMapSource` without an inner map directly borrows its supplied map and therefore does","+A bare `SourceMapSource` without an inner map shares its supplied map and therefore does"," not normalize it for `columns: false`. Wrapping or combining it forces the specialized streaming"," paths."," ","@@ -198,16 +197,38 @@ to the scalar's starting byte."," "," ### `SourceMap`"," ","-Source maps mainly come from parsed JSON or a `Source` graph. `SourceMap` uses `Cow` fields to reuse","-strings owned by these inputs instead of cloning them:","-","-- `from_bytes` retains the JSON buffer that parsed fields borrow from;","-- computed maps borrow strings from the source graph, and `into_static(owner)` retains that owner;","-- `as_borrowed` creates a cheap borrowed view.","-- `sources_content` entries use `Option<Cow<str>>`: `None` is missing content (JSON `null`),","-  while `Some(\"\")` is an explicitly empty source. Preserve this distinction through parsing,","-  streaming, serialization, and persistent cache. Omit `sourcesContent` only when all entries","-  are missing; map builders keep present arrays aligned with `sources`.","+Source maps mainly come from parsed JSON or a `Source` graph. `SourceMap` owns UTF-8","+`bytes_str::BytesStr` fields independently of those inputs:","+","+- `from_bytes` parses the input Vec mutably, then transfers it to `Bytes::from_owner` while","+  retaining the borrowed tape. It directly constructs owning `BytesStr` slices with `slice_ref`,","+  without intermediate range arrays. A local raw slice separates the parser borrow from the","+  Vec header; the tape is dropped before its owner on return and unwind. Do not replace","+  `from_owner` with `Bytes::from(Vec)`: a Box conversion can invalidate the tape's references.","+  Duplicate known fields use the DOM fallback to preserve simd-json's duplicate-key behavior.","+  Escaped strings share the input allocation too.","+- `OnSource` and `OnName` borrow `BytesStr` handles for each callback. Leaves and transforms","+  forward references; collectors clone only when retaining text in deduplication tables, maps,","+  or caches. Joined source-root paths may be temporary, so references cannot escape the callback.","+  Resulting maps own their handles without copying source contents or retaining a Source graph.","+- all fields live directly in `SourceMap`, which derives `Serialize`. Clones and `as_borrowed`","+  clone text/array handles; setters replace individual fields without copying unchanged text.","+  Nonempty immutable arrays use `ThinArc<(), T>`, with elements and metadata in one allocation;","+  empty `sources`, `sourcesContent`, and `names` fields do not allocate. Builders freeze their Vecs by moving handles, while","+  infallible exact-size iterators can initialize the shared array directly. Fallible parsing","+  reserves the tape array's known length before collecting. Text bytes remain shared. Serialize","+  and hash the slices,","+  preserving the array representation and excluding ThinArc's internal length/header from hashes.","+- `set_sources_content` with an empty vector detaches remaining metadata, because a small shared","+  JSON slice would otherwise keep the removed contents' allocation alive. Nonempty arrays,","+  including arrays of missing entries, only replace the shared contents array.","+","+There is no SourceMap lifetime extension or Source owner. `map()` returns an owned map;","+generated text can be released when its Source is otherwise no longer referenced.","+`sources_content` entries use `Option<BytesStr>`: `None` is missing content (JSON `null`),","+while `Some(\"\")` is an explicitly empty source. Preserve this distinction through parsing,","+streaming, serialization, and persistent cache. Omit `sourcesContent` only when all entries","+are missing; map builders keep present arrays aligned with `sources`."," "," ## 4. Source types and file map"," ","@@ -223,7 +244,7 @@ representation optimizations."," | `RawStringSource` | text leaf            | no mappings; use `from_static` for literals                         |"," | `RawBufferSource` | binary leaf          | exact bytes; lazy lossy rope view                                   |"," | `OriginalSource`  | mapped text leaf     | lazily creates token-like or line mappings                          |","-| `SourceMapSource` | existing/nested map  | directly borrows one map or composes outer and inner maps           |","+| `SourceMapSource` | existing/nested map  | shares one map or composes outer and inner maps                     |"," | `MappingSource`   | external map JSON    | retains the original map and serializes JSON on demand              |"," | `ConcatSource`    | ordered composition  | flattens nested concats, merges adjacent raw strings, remaps tables |"," | `ReplaceSource`   | byte-range transform | maintains sorted edits and repairs mappings                         |","@@ -233,9 +254,9 @@ Important implementation details:"," "," - `OriginalSource` splits potential JavaScript tokens with `memchr`; it is not an AST tokenizer."," - `SourceMapSource` composition indexes inner mappings by line and binary-searches the closest","-  preceding segment. Avoid cloning maps or eagerly splitting all `sourcesContent`.","+  preceding segment. Avoid rebuilding shared maps or eagerly splitting all `sourcesContent`."," - `MappingSource` is the JSON asset itself, so `map()` returns `None`. It retains the original","-  `SourceMap` and its owner without interning, deduplicating, or rewriting `sourcesContent`.","+  `SourceMap` without interning, deduplicating, or rewriting `sourcesContent`.","   Unedited `source()` and `buffer()` use the existing `SourceMap::to_json()` serializer on demand","   and cache only its byte length. Construction must not scan the map to compute its exact JSON","   size; `size()` computes it lazily if needed, and this cache must not affect equality or hashing.","@@ -329,9 +350,9 @@ cache."," "," The same owner-retention pattern appears in other narrowly scoped `unsafe` paths:"," ","-- `SourceMap::from_bytes` keeps the parsed byte buffer alive;","-- `SourceMap::into_static` keeps the owning `BoxSource` alive;","-- `SourceContentLines` stores line views while retaining the backing `Cow<str>`;","+- `SourceMap::from_bytes` keeps the parsed tape and its Vec owner together until all strings","+  have become independently owning `BytesStr` s